Wrote the coder-3.json file with one row for Gail Griffin / data-centers. HB2756 (2026) — which she prime-sponsored and voted Yes on, letting the Corporation Commission set cost-allocation terms for "extra high load factor customers" — shows direction toward protecting residential ratepayers but doesn't match any single rung's full clause set (no outright cost-pass-through bar, no impact assessments/community benefits, no permitting/transparency provisions), so I coded it BLANK `direction-only` and flagged the need for her own words tying the vote to a specific rung.
